### TimeProvider (.NET 8)
{{TimeProvider}} abstracts the clock and timers: {{GetUtcNow()}}, {{GetTimestamp()}}, {{CreateTimer()}}, and async {{Task.Delay(span, timeProvider)}}. Production uses {{TimeProvider.System}}; tests use {{FakeTimeProvider}} (Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing) and call {{Advance()}} to move time instantly. This makes cut-off times, token expiry, retry delays, SLA timers and end-of-day logic testable without sleeping or flaky timing.

### Source-generated logging
{{[LoggerMessage]}} on a partial method generates the logging code at compile time:
- no boxing of value-type arguments and no params array allocation;
- the {{IsEnabled}} check happens before any formatting work;
- event ids and message templates are fixed and analysable;
- works with redaction attributes ({{[PersonalData]}}) and enrichment.
Compared with {{logger.LogInformation($"...")}} (string interpolation formats even when the level is disabled and destroys structured properties), it is both faster and more correct.

